From ebb318299c2c9fdc612ed74a55c548928093e7fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ga=C3=ABl=20Duval?= <gael@murena.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:50:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] feat(documenteditor): Word paste options

- Paste becomes a split button: the main part pastes, the arrow opens
  "Paste Options:" with Keep Source Formatting (K), Merge Formatting (M)
  and Keep Text Only (T), with Fluent icons; choosing one pastes and
  switches the paste to that option.
- The main part no longer shows the "copy, cut and paste" warning when
  the asynchronous Clipboard API pastes: the warning appears only if
  nothing was pasted after 1.5 s.
- Paste Options chip after a paste: Word's labels, keys and icons, and
  the Merge Formatting (M) and Use Destination Styles (S) options that
  the chip of DocumentHolder did not label or bind.
The Toolbar view only gets split/menu on the big Paste button; the rest
lives in DE.Controllers.WordFormatting. Format Painter already behaves
like Word (one click: once, double click: until Esc or a new click) and
is unchanged. Strings in en, fr, de, es, it, pt, pt-pt, nl, ru, pl, ja,
zh.

[branding]

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
